  "controls": "A multivariate regression model will be used to control for potential confounders. Covariates will include: game context (quarter, score differential, time remaining in shot clock), player identity (PNR ball handler, PNR screener), team identity, opponent defensive rating, whether the preceding drive resulted in a shot attempt, and whether the drive was successful (e.g., score, assist, drawn foul). Player and team fixed effects will be considered to account for unobserved heterogeneity.",
  "falsification": "A falsification test will involve analyzing the PPP of PNRs preceded by a drive that occurred significantly earlier in the possession (e.g., more than 5 seconds prior, or separated by another distinct play type). We would expect no significant effect in this case. Additionally, we could test for an effect on defensive plays preceding a PNR, which should also yield no effect.",
  "multiplicity": "No multiple testing correction is planned as this is a single, focused hypothesis. If exploratory analyses lead to additional hypotheses, those will be noted as such.",
  "decision_rule": "The hypothesis will be considered 'supported' if the estimated coefficient for 'Teammate_Drive_Precedes' is positive and statistically significant (p < 0.05) in the primary regression model, after controlling for confounders. It will be 'rejected' if the coefficient is not significantly different from zero or is negative. The magnitude and practical significance of the effect will also be considered.",
  "data_version": "NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25, and 2025-26 (complete regular seasons and playoffs where available) using derived play-type possession records from the graph database and raw play-by-play data for sequence identification."
 }

